OL,3,GNEWSAMurder victim's medical records
OL,4,Awrongfully accessed
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe parents of a murdered woman have
OL,7,Fsaid they are devastated after her
OL,8,Fdigital medical records were accessed
OL,9,Fby staff without authorisation.
OL,11,FMichaela Hall, 49, from Mount Hawke, in
OL,12,Fnorth Cornwall, was killed in 2021 by
OL,13,Fher partner Lee Kendall who was later
OL,14,Fjailed for a minimum of 21 years.
OL,16,FHer parents said they were informed by
OL,17,FRoyal Cornwall Hospitals NHS Trust
OL,18,F(RCHT) her records were accessed on
OL,19,Fmultiple occasions over several years
OL,20,Fwith one person accessing them seven
OL,21,Ftimes including on what would have been
OL,22,Fher birthday.
OL,23,APub: 01-OctQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBW-SW Eng NewsC Reg TVFWeather
FL,344,340,200,160,0,100
